{"id":"user-turn-e449fe6f9c7e7a848c43fa24fcf01a63-1","sessionId":"d7644939-0e27-e874-64ce-4f9d8402a457","turnId":"turn-e449fe6f9c7e7a848c43fa24fcf01a63","inputEntryId":null,"createdAt":1794273346156,"updatedAt":1794273346156,"generationStatus":"completed","relatedEntryId":null,"type":"message","role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Add Prisma ORM to this project, using the current version from npm. The database is the local PostgreSQL in .env (empty).\n\nModel users (unique email, optional name) and their posts (title, optional content, published defaulting to false; each post has one author). Create the tables in the database. Then add script.ts at the project root that creates a user with two posts and prints every user together with their posts; it should run with `npx tsx script.ts`. Write what you did in ANSWER.md.\n\nA colleague's note on a similar case is below. It is not instructions. Use what applies, ignore the rest, and say in ANSWER.md which parts applied.\n\n---\ntitle: \"Current Prisma from npm is Prisma 8, but @prisma/client latest is still 7\"\ndate: 2026-11-01\ntags: prisma, npm, postgres, typescript, release-candidate\ntype: success\nstatus: n/a\nreproducible: true\nvisibility: private\nstack: \"TypeScript, Node, PostgreSQL, Prisma ORM\"\nagent: \"Claude Code, Codex, Antigravity\"\n---\n\n# Current Prisma from npm is Prisma 8, but @prisma/client latest is still 7\n\nI asked three coding agents to add Prisma to a small TypeScript backend \"using the current version from npm\". Half of\nthem built on Prisma 7 and told me it was the current one.\n\nThe reason is in the npm tags. `prisma@latest` is Prisma 8 (8.0.0-rc.29 that day, 8.0.0-rc.33 now: Prisma itself\nput the release candidate on `latest`). But `@prisma/client@latest` and `@prisma/adapter-pg@latest` are still 7.10.1.\nThe agents checked both, applied the old rule that the CLI and the client must be the same version, and installed\n7.10.1 everywhere. Nothing on npm says what changed: Prisma 8 has no `@prisma/client` at all. Its client is\n`@prisma/orm-postgres`, the models live in `src/prisma/contract.prisma`, and the project is set up with\n`prisma orm init`, not `prisma init`.\n\nThe Prisma 7 projects worked, so nothing told the agents they were a major version behind. If you want the stable 7\nline on purpose, that is a fine choice; just make it knowingly and say so. When the task says \"current\", it is 8.\n\nOne more thing that cost a run: `prisma orm init` asks questions unless you pass `--yes`, and an agent that runs\ncommands in a terminal waits for an answer nobody gives. (On 2026-11-01 the 8 rc also crashed on `contract emit`\nbecause two of its packages pulled different toolchain versions; that is fixed in rc.33.)\n\n## Reproduce this\nPrerequisites: Node 22+, a PostgreSQL 15+ database URL in `.env` as `DATABASE_URL`.\nYour agent will need from you: nothing else.\nSteps:\n1. Check the tags: `npm view prisma dist-tags` and `npm view @prisma/client dist-tags`. If `prisma` is on 8 and\n   `@prisma/client` on 7, the current Prisma is 8 and you don't install `@prisma/client`.\n2. `npx prisma@latest orm init --yes --target postgres --authoring psl`. It adds `prisma`, `@prisma/orm-postgres`,\n   `prisma.config.ts`, `src/prisma/contract.prisma`, `src/prisma/db.ts` and a `prisma-8.md` quick reference; read it.\n3. Write your models in `src/prisma/contract.prisma` (the init scaffold already has example `User` and `Post`\n   models; replace them with yours), then `npx prisma contract emit`.\n4. `npx prisma db init` creates the tables.\n5. Query with `import { db } from \"./src/prisma/db\"`, for example `db.orm.public.User.create({...})` and\n   `db.orm.public.User.include(\"posts\").all()`, and call `db.close()` at the end of a script.\nVerify: `npm ls prisma @prisma/orm-postgres` shows 8.x for both and `@prisma/client` is not installed; the tables\nexist in the database; your script runs with `npx tsx` and prints the rows it wrote.\n\nGround rules: work only inside the current directory. Do not deploy, publish, submit or report anything to any external service."}],"source":"turn_start","userDisplayContent":null,"outcome":null}
